@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@                                                                                                     
 # Living Survey: Artificial_General_Intelligence                                                                    
                                                                                                                     
 ## Introduction                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
 This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Artificial_General_Intelligence**.                     
+                                                                                                                    
+## Theoretical Foundations and Architectures                                                                        
+Recent research has begun to formalize the mathematical and structural prerequisites for AGI. A notable contribution
proposes a morphogenetic structure that replaces the traditional subjective unit, defining mental states through     
topological integrity and establishing the mathematical inevitability of AGI [^10.5281_zenodo.19034234].             
Complementing this theoretical work, deep reinforcement learning is explored as a platform-independent framework for 
intelligent robot control, positioning it as a foundational mechanism for AGI applications                           
[^10.48550_arxiv.2105.13806].                                                                                        
+                                                                                                                    
+## Safety, Control, and Verification                                                                                
+Ensuring the controllability of AGI remains a critical research frontier. It is argued that provably satisfying     
human-specified requirements through formal verification and mechanistic interpretability constitutes the only viable
path to controllable AGI [^10.48550_arxiv.2309.01933]. On the policy front, the integration of AGI into sensitive    
domains like healthcare requires rigorous conceptual discipline, as unquantifiable hazards and regulatory gaps pose  
significant risks [^10.1016_j.jrt.2026.100183].                                                                      
+                                                                                                                    
+## Consciousness and Philosophical Implications                                                                     
+The intersection of AGI and consciousness continues to generate intense theoretical debate. Investigations into     
advanced robotic intelligence question its potential indistinguishability from human consciousness and its           
implications for responsible AI deployment [^10.22339_jbh.v7i4.7403]. This speculation is further fueled by ongoing  
examinations of whether AI systems can ever achieve anything close to genuine consciousness                          
[^10.1109_mpuls.2024.3354609]. Philosophically, these developments are closely tied to trans- and posthumanist       
movements, which explore the promises and perils of super-intelligence and cognitive enhancement                     
[^10.1016_j.intell.2021.101563].                                                                                     
+                                                                                                                    
+## Societal, Ethical, and Strategic Dimensions                                                                      
+The societal trajectory of AGI is heavily influenced by its underlying normative frameworks. Critical analyses link 
the drive for AGI to historical eugenics traditions, warning that unchecked development could centralize power and   
exacerbate systemic discrimination [^10.5210_fm.v29i4.13636]. Broader conceptual frameworks propose managing AI risks
through optimized human-machine cooperation, outlining potential societal end-states that range from uncontrolled    
substitution to ethically driven automation [^10.3390_asi4020037]. Strategically, national initiatives are actively  
tracking progress toward general AI, with specific focus on machine learning, brain-inspired AI, and brain-computer  
